WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.599 --> 00:00:03.649
Brace yourselves — the Cable guy is coming!

00:00:03.649 --> 00:00:07.779
Ever since the post-credits tease at the end
of the smash hit Deadpool, comic book fans

00:00:07.779 --> 00:00:11.120
have been excitedly awaiting the arrival of
Cable.

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:14.490
"Oh, but I can tell you one thing and it's
a bit of a secret.

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:17.870
For the sequel, we're gonna have Cable."

00:00:17.870 --> 00:00:21.950
And ever since that post credits tease, non-comic
book fans have been wondering, who the heck

00:00:21.950 --> 00:00:23.110
is Cable!?

00:00:23.110 --> 00:00:27.330
Well, we're about to answer that question
for you, because here's a dangerously in-depth

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:31.400
look at everything Marvel fans need to know
about Marvel's most complicated mutant.

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:33.440
[Singing] "Who the f--- is that?

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:35.020
He's a man out of time!

00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:36.080
Who the f--- is that?

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:37.780
He likes to fight crime!

00:00:37.860 --> 00:00:38.900
It's f---in' Cable!"

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:41.010
Convoluted history

00:00:41.010 --> 00:00:45.359
If you thought X-Men: Days of Future Past
was confusing, grab a bottle of aspirin and

00:00:45.359 --> 00:00:50.420
lie down, because Cable's convoluted history
makes that film look like child's play.

00:00:50.420 --> 00:00:54.829
Which is fitting, because Cable began messing
up X-Men continuity from the moment he was

00:00:54.829 --> 00:00:55.829
born.

00:00:55.829 --> 00:01:00.609
See, Cable is actually Nathan Summers, the
son of Scott Summers - aka Cyclops - and a

00:01:00.609 --> 00:01:04.840
lady named Madeline Pryor, who was actually
an evil clone of Jean Grey.

00:01:04.840 --> 00:01:09.439
Cyclops and the real Jean Grey then raised
Nathan for all of a hot minute before Apocalypse

00:01:09.439 --> 00:01:14.640
infected the baby with the techno virus, a
disease that turns flesh into parasitic robotic

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:15.640
circuitry.

00:01:15.640 --> 00:01:19.490
In order to save him, Cyclops and Jean gave
him to a time traveling prophet from the distant

00:01:19.490 --> 00:01:23.979
future named Mother Askani, who was actually
their daughter from an alternate universe.

00:01:23.979 --> 00:01:29.369
It was tragic, but then Scott and Jeansent
their consciousnesses into the future as well,

00:01:29.369 --> 00:01:33.260
inhabiting host bodies in order to secretly
raise their son in the future without his

00:01:33.260 --> 00:01:34.260
knowledge.

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:35.700
So… yay?

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:40.650
After he became an adult, Cable spent decades
time traveling around history, battling the

00:01:40.650 --> 00:01:42.250
forces of Apocalypse.

00:01:42.250 --> 00:01:46.369
As a grizzled old man, he finally returned
to the time period of his birth and became

00:01:46.369 --> 00:01:51.109
leader of the New Mutants, turning them into
a paramilitary mutant team called X-Force.

00:01:51.109 --> 00:01:56.039
Eventually, he revealed his purpose was to
protect a messiah baby who was supposed to

00:01:56.039 --> 00:01:57.869
save mutantkind.

00:01:57.869 --> 00:02:01.950
He adopted her, naming her Hope, and then
did a bunch of time-travel-y things to protect

00:02:01.950 --> 00:02:04.259
her from other folks who wanted to get her.

00:02:04.259 --> 00:02:09.030
This is important, because clues in the Deadpool
2 trailer - like Cable's teddy bear - suggest

00:02:09.030 --> 00:02:12.610
that protecting Hope may be a major part of
the plot for the film.

00:02:12.610 --> 00:02:13.620
Got all that?

00:02:13.620 --> 00:02:17.420
Good, because things are about to get even
more confusing…

00:02:17.420 --> 00:02:19.550
Clones and doppelgangers

00:02:19.550 --> 00:02:23.780
Considering his mother was an evil clone of
Jean Grey, it's only fitting that Cable himself

00:02:23.780 --> 00:02:25.770
also has an evil clone.

00:02:25.770 --> 00:02:30.160
Named Stryfe, Cable's clone was kidnapped
at a young age by Apocalypse and raised to

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:34.360
become the vessel for Apocalypse's consciousness
when his current host body died.

00:02:34.360 --> 00:02:38.920
That didn't work out, however, so Stryfe got
to just be an evil Cable instead, but with

00:02:38.920 --> 00:02:41.130
a really cool giant helmet.

00:02:41.130 --> 00:02:46.310
Not quite so cool is Nate Grey, the X-Man,
an alternate universe version of Cable whose

00:02:46.310 --> 00:02:49.260
mom was actually the real Jean Grey.

00:02:49.260 --> 00:02:53.330
This Nate never got the metal arm and stuff,
but he did get a bitchin' 90's haircut and

00:02:53.330 --> 00:02:55.180
jacket, so we'll call that even.

00:02:55.180 --> 00:02:58.380
Honestly, you know what, we can't even figure
out this crap anymore.

00:02:58.380 --> 00:03:01.320
Just pretend it makes sense and let's move
on.

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:02.520
Convoluted powers

00:03:02.520 --> 00:03:07.430
If you're wondering just what Cable's actual
powers are, you're not alone, as they're almost

00:03:07.430 --> 00:03:09.140
as confusing as his backstory.

00:03:09.140 --> 00:03:14.140
Thanks to his mom, he inherited extremely
powerful telekinetic and telepathic abilities.

00:03:14.140 --> 00:03:18.750
However, he often can't use either, because
those powers are entirely spent keeping the

00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:21.920
techno virus from turning him into a full-on
robot.

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:25.310
Don't worry, though, because he has other
powers, at least... sometimes.

00:03:25.310 --> 00:03:30.110
While he usually uses a time machine to travel
through the ages, sometimes he can just...

00:03:30.110 --> 00:03:33.750
do it himself, and other times he can predict
the future as well.

00:03:33.750 --> 00:03:38.550
His robot arm also gives him super strength,
and he has a ton of super-advanced guns from

00:03:38.550 --> 00:03:41.060
the future, which he loves shooting people
with.

00:03:41.060 --> 00:03:45.420
And sometimes one of his eyes glows for no
apparent reason, which is a fantastic party

00:03:45.420 --> 00:03:46.540
trick.

00:03:46.540 --> 00:03:47.900
Straight man

00:03:47.900 --> 00:03:52.730
Cable is a grim and gritty avatar of deadly
serious earnestness, which makes him a perfect

00:03:52.730 --> 00:03:56.970
foil for Deadpool, who is… you know, exactly
the opposite in every way.

00:03:56.970 --> 00:04:01.790
The one thing they do have in common, though,
is they both love guns, not to mention superfluous

00:04:01.790 --> 00:04:03.300
pouches on their costumes.

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:06.960
As a straight man for Deadpool to play off
of, Cable has no equal.

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:10.200
"The survival of Earth entirely depends on…"

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:12.460
"Wah wah wah wah."

00:04:12.460 --> 00:04:14.520
The long road to the big screen

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:19.030
After Cable was teased at the end of Deadpool,
the big question for fans was: who is going

00:04:19.030 --> 00:04:20.079
to play him?

00:04:20.079 --> 00:04:22.750
Finding the answer turned out to be quite
a saga.

00:04:22.750 --> 00:04:27.440
While fans rallied behind Avatar's Stephen
Lang, rumors claimed that Deadpool director

00:04:27.440 --> 00:04:31.830
Tim Miller's insistence on casting Kyle Chandler
in the role led to his ultimate departure

00:04:31.830 --> 00:04:33.370
from the franchise.

00:04:33.370 --> 00:04:37.790
Miller denied this, but the production reportedly
considered everyone from Brad Pitt to David

00:04:37.790 --> 00:04:41.240
Harbour in the role before finally landing
on Josh Brolin.

00:04:41.240 --> 00:04:44.390
And Brolin is pumped for the role, both literally
and figuratively.

00:04:44.390 --> 00:04:49.440
"There's a lot of stuff going on in Deadpool
that's very surprising, and that will be very

00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:51.160
satisfying when you see it.

00:04:51.160 --> 00:04:53.500
To me, it's even funnier than the first one."

00:04:53.500 --> 00:04:54.730
We can't wait!

00:04:54.730 --> 00:04:56.290
Thanks for watching!

00:04:56.290 --> 00:04:58.700
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:04:58.700 --> 00:05:00.450
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

